Z||000008||8Ball||08-04-2001||11:49 PM||||I have come up with the Perfect sound system.<BR>And I just tested it out on my Hyundai. Sounded SWEET!!!<P>Ok this is going to sound like a mix between Redneck and Computer Geek... but then I am a Tech in Tennessee  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Altec sells a speaker set for computers that has 4 satellites and a sub. Well I wanted to see what it would sound like in a car, seeing as how in my house it sounds better then a rather expensive stereo I have. Got it all hooked up by tieing the front speaker wires from the radio to a female end of a headphone jack, Then the same with he rear speakers. Then just plug them in and position the speakers. As for power you will need a voltage converter so you can plug in the sub.<P>When you finish with a little work and even less money (like 300 bucks) you can have a Bose like system that will hit harder than most 1000-2000 dollar systems  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and it will ALL fit in a Fiero with ease. Hmm I bet I could make a really neat set. Hmmmm work to be done  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>8ball<P><BR>P.S. I know it sounds crazy but the shape of the speakers would really suit a Fiero int.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Philphine||08-05-2001||12:09 PM||||i understand the terminology pretty much. electronics degree and military electronics certificate. car stereo has always been a hobby. put my first system in 21 yrs. ago (deck and 2 in my old hornet). i think i can put in a pretty well balanced system, but sometimes "i jus gots to get mah thump awnnn". <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>SERENITY NOW!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000010||Boomtastic||08-05-2001||01:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackDragon:<BR><B>check out this site <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Interior/Interior.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Interior/Interior.html</A> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Stick with AusFiero's center console. It is built to handle the 10" sub, has the volume, and is $150 cheaper, plus free shipping to US/Canada & AU.<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
